 {"id":"fabro-8208","title":"gofib: add -limit flag to cap output size safely","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-24T16:14:54.720Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-24T16:31:03.919Z","description":"## Goal\n\nA `-limit <int>` flag: hard cap on the LARGEST index gofib will print,\nindependent of `-start`/`-n`. Protects against accidental huge output\nwhen `-n` is large (e.g. `-n 100000` should still stop at the limit).\n\n## Semantics\n\n- `-limit <int>`: do not print any index > limit. Default: no limit.\n- Combines with `-start` and `-n`: the effective output is the\n  intersection of all three (start <= index <= limit, at most -n lines).\n- Validation mirrors existing flags: values < 0 exit non-zero with a\n  stderr error message.\n- `-limit` smaller than `-start` produces empty output (zero lines),\n  NOT an error — document this in the README.\n- `-json` and `-pretty` combine as usual on the reduced set.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Flag parsed via the flag package; `Fib(n)` stays the only computation\n  (no inline recomputation — CONTEXT.md).\n- Table-driven tests: default (no limit), limit caps large -n, limit+start\n  intersection, limit < start gives empty output and exit 0, negative\n  limit rejected, limit with -json and -pretty.\n- README.md flag table gains the `-limit` row with a REAL example\n  invocation and its actual output (capture from the built binary, do not\n  invent output).\n- `just qualitygate` green","closedAt":"2026-08-24T16:31:03.919Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-cfb6","title":"gofib: add -seed flag for reproducible index selection","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-24T19:15:32.840Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-24T22:24:06.679Z","description":"## Goal\n\nA `-seed <int>` flag: print ONLY the Fibonacci number at a given index\n(one line) — a tiny lookup mode instead of a range, for spot-checks and\nscripting against specific indices.\n\n## Semantics\n\n- `-seed i` prints exactly one entry for index `i` in the active output\n  mode: text mode `i: <value>`; JSON mode one object\n  `{\"index\":i,\"fib\":\"<string>\"}`; pretty mode single-row alignment.\n- `-seed` overrides the RANGE flags: with `-seed 10 -n 5 -start 2` only\n  index 10 prints (exactly one line). Document that precedence in the\n  README row.\n- `-version` keeps its top precedence (existing behavior, README pins\n  it).\n- Validation mirrors the other flags: values < 0 exit non-zero with a\n  stderr error. `-seed 0` behaves like `-start 0`: treated as unset\n  (sentinel), so plain `gofib` output stays unchanged.\n- `Fib(n)` stays the only computation — no inline recomputation\n  (CONTEXT.md).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Table-driven tests: single index via -seed; -seed overrides -n/-start\n  (and -limit); -seed 0 sentinel; -seed with -json and -pretty;\n  negative rejected; -version still wins.\n- README.md flag table gains the `-seed` row with a REAL example\n  invocation and its actual output (capture from the built binary, do\n  not invent output); the precedence note lives in that row.\n- `just qualitygate` green","closedAt":"2026-08-24T22:24:06.679Z"}
 {"id":"fabro-d920","title":"gofib: add -format flag for compact table output","status":"closed","type":"task","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-24T22:19:17.606Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-24T22:30:02.942Z","description":"## Goal\n\nA `-format <mode>` flag selecting the OUTPUT STYLE globally, unifying\nthe text/json/pretty matrix: `text` (default), `json`, `pretty`, and a\nnew compact `table` mode (no leading index column, values only, one\nper line).\n\n## Semantics\n\n- `-format text|json|pretty|table` — invalid values exit non-zero with\n  a stderr error listing valid modes.\n- `-json` and `-pretty` remain as SHORTCUTS: `-json` == `-format json`,\n  `-pretty` == `-format pretty`. If BOTH a shortcut and `-format` are\n  given and they conflict (e.g. `-pretty -format json`), exit non-zero\n  with a clear error — no silent precedence.\n- `table` mode: values only, one per line (aligned, right-justified to\n  the widest value). Composes with `-start`/`-n`/`-limit` as usual.\n- `-version` still wins over everything.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Flag via the flag package; existing behavior for `-json`/`-pretty`\n  UNCHANGED (regression tests pin them).\n- Table-driven tests: each mode, shortcut==format equivalence, conflict\n  rejection, invalid mode rejection, table+start/n/limit combos.\n- README flag table gains the `-format` row with a REAL example per\n  mode (capture from the built binary; do not invent output).\n- `just qualitygate` green","closedAt":"2026-08-24T22:30:02.942Z"}
-{"id":"fabro-f74b","title":"gofib: -sum flag printing the checksum of the selected range","status":"open","type":"feature","priority":2,"createdAt":"2026-08-25T13:23:37.817Z","updatedAt":"2026-08-25T13:23:37.817Z","description":"## Goal\n\nA `-sum` flag: instead of printing one number per line, print exactly one\nline containing the sum of all Fibonacci numbers in the selected range.\nNatural next flag after -limit: it exercises range selection (-start,\n-limit, -n) with a different aggregation and keeps the loop testing the\nsame surface (flag parsing, validation, format modes, README, tests).\n\n## Semantics\n\n- `-sum` (bool, default false): when set, gofib prints one line with the\n  sum of the numbers it WOULD have printed (the same intersection of\n  -start/-limit/-n that line mode uses).\n- Output format follows the selected mode: text prints `sum: <value>`;\n  json prints one JSON object {\"index_range\":[first,last],\"sum\":\"<value>\"}\n  (sum as string, it can exceed int64); pretty/table print the bare value.\n- `-seed` with `-sum` is an error: -seed already collapses the range to one\n  index; exit non-zero with a stderr message naming both flags.\n- Zero selected numbers (e.g. -limit < -start): sum prints 0, no error —\n  mirrors -limit semantics.\n- `-version` precedence is unchanged.\n- Values stay big.Int end to end (CONTEXT.md: Fib(n) stays the only\n  Fibonacci computation; the sum accumulates big.Ints, no float/string math).\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Flag parsed via the flag package; validation mirrors existing flags.\n- Table-driven tests: default range sum, sum with -start/-limit narrowing,\n  empty range -> 0, -seed + -sum rejected, each format mode renders the sum,\n  -version precedence.\n- README: -sum documented in the flag reference with one example line.\n- Gate green (format, vet, build, test).","labels":["product"]}
